WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.210
One rule I heard is if
you can look at something

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:07.411
and you haven't worn it
for a year, it should go.

00:00:07.411 --> 00:00:08.244
Yeah.

00:00:08.244 --> 00:00:09.740
And I have the same rule with people.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:10.780
(laughing)

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:11.670
Oh no!

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:13.589
Yeah and relatives.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:14.422
If I haven't, if I haven't.

00:00:14.422 --> 00:00:15.255
Relatives.

00:00:15.255 --> 00:00:16.270
Spoken to the, yeah.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:20.420
People in my life, one of
my brothers, we haven't,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.700
and there's nothing personal,
we just are both busy.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.630
We haven't really talked
and it's been almost a year.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.120
And if we get to a year, I'll
never speak to him again.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.030
He's outta my life.

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.130
Canceled. Harsh, but okay.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:34.700
No, you know, and guess
what, I'm fond of him.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.230
And he's a really good guy.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:37.406
Yeah.

00:00:37.406 --> 00:00:39.030
But it's just been a while.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:39.863
It's been almost, it's
been about 11 months

00:00:39.863 --> 00:00:42.803
and probably 11 months and two weeks.

00:00:44.295 --> 00:00:45.370
But who's counting?

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:48.383
Yeah. But if two more weeks go by,

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.240
I'll never speak to Justin again.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.552
That's it.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.810
You've got two other ones. It's fine.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:55.390
Yeah, exactly.

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:58.717
And guess what, Justin may be
my favorite of all of them.

00:00:58.717 --> 00:00:59.727
(laughing)

00:00:59.727 --> 00:01:01.029
That sucks for him.

00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:01.862
So that... it's tragic.

00:01:01.862 --> 00:01:02.695
But yeah.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.560
And for me, he's actually, I
don't think it sucks for him.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.070
It sucks for me because
he's a wonderful person.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:09.376
He's great. He's gotta, I like his.

00:01:09.376 --> 00:01:10.240
Why don't you reach out to him?

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.210
Because I set up this rule.

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.214
He's been avoiding you for
a year so this could happen.

00:01:16.214 --> 00:01:17.620
[Conan] That's true.

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:18.453
Yeah.

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:19.520
Maybe he planned this out.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.150
I think he planned it out.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:23.400
Several times I've called him to say hi

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.403
and someone's picked up the
phone who sounded like Justin.

00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:27.236
(laughing)

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:29.060
And then when I say, hey,
it's Conan, they quick,

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.229
it sounds to me like their voice changes.

00:01:32.229 --> 00:01:36.503
And suddenly it's this
Greek, an old Greek man.

00:01:36.503 --> 00:01:37.400
laughing)

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:40.653
Saying that Mr. Justin is not here.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:43.180
And I'm like, who are you?

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:45.960
And he is like, I fish
for the fish in the sea.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.363
I am the fisherman.

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:49.671
And then he hangs up.

00:01:49.671 --> 00:01:50.650
(laughing)

00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.820
Do you think it's possible
that that's Justin?

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.948
Yeah. You're being reverse catfished.

00:01:55.948 --> 00:01:56.781
Yeah.

00:01:56.781 --> 00:01:57.940
You're being fish-catted.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:58.773
I know.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.070
I'm the, I'm the first person
to be reverse catfished

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.620
in this modern era.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.018
And guess what?

00:02:07.018 --> 00:02:08.450
It happens a lot.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:10.720
I talk to a lot of people who I call

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:12.470
and I just want to connect to them.

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.240
Like, you know, my old writing partner,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:16.110
Greg Daniels and I'll be
like, hey Greg, how you doing?

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.160
And it sounds like Greg,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:22.160
but once I identify myself,
suddenly he's Portuguese.

00:02:22.162 --> 00:02:22.995
Somehow.

00:02:24.437 --> 00:02:26.470
And he sells pans for a living.

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:27.870
I didn't know you could do this.

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:30.141
I'm gonna have to implement some changes.

00:02:30.141 --> 00:02:31.610
(laughing)

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:34.460
Yeah. The next time I
try and talk to Matt,

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.140
I'm just gonna come onto
this podcast in a mustache.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.040
Who are you gonna be
when I call you, Matt?

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:40.720
And I say, Hey, Matt, this is it's me.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.010
It's Conan.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.970
(speaking gibberish

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.200
(laughing)

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.033
Oh, okay.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.930
Well I'm sorry, but when Matt does come by

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:50.941
could you tell him that Conan called?

00:02:50.941 --> 00:02:54.608
(speaking gibberish)

00:02:56.591 --> 00:02:57.430
Okay, all right. Well, very good.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:02:59.450
Hey, maybe I'll try and call Sona now.

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.780
Hey, Sona. How are you?

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.010
It's Conan.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.639
Let's chat.

00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:07.908
(speaking Armenian)

00:03:07.908 --> 00:03:11.160
(laughing)

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:12.358
[Conan] Wow.

00:03:12.358 --> 00:03:14.467
(speaking Armenian)

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:17.350
(laughing)

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.500
Is that Armenian or are
you doing an impression

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:21.360
of Andy Kaufman as Latka?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.390
Or are you running a tape backwards?

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:24.758
Yeah

00:03:24.758 --> 00:03:25.690
(speaking gibberish)

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.570
Those are actual, real Armenian words.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:28.550
Thank you very much.

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.057
I, yeah, I actually used my
Armenian for the first time.

00:03:32.057 --> 00:03:35.000
Yeah, you just said, please,
may I have more dried

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.550
and pressed apricot?

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:37.501
Okay.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.580
(laughing)

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:40.413
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:40.413 --> 00:03:43.110
Or did you say dried
or pressed pomegranate?

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:45.170
I'm sorry, they were, I
was offered two things

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.641
while I was there for
dessert and that was it.

00:03:47.641 --> 00:03:48.474
(laughing)

00:03:48.474 --> 00:03:49.307
They both.

00:03:49.307 --> 00:03:50.880
You're actually, you're right.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.880
That's pretty much all
the dessert we have.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:52.980
Both times!

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.340
I was like, what do you have for dessert?

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:57.100
This is when I took Sona
to Armenia, both times.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:57.933
And I loved it there.

00:03:57.933 --> 00:04:00.100
I love the Armenian people

00:04:01.844 --> 00:04:03.520
(laughing)

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:05.343
But both times I was,

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.260
okay, let's look at that dessert menu.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:10.234
And they would say what menu?

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.067
Yeah.

00:04:11.067 --> 00:04:12.540
You can you can have a
dried pressed apricot

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:14.090
or a dried pressed pomegranate.

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:15.540
Yeah, that's it.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.503
And I wonder why anybody
would avoid you for a year.

00:04:18.503 --> 00:04:21.086
(laughing)

